Files taken, from the jars:
  datascript/util.cljc, lru.cljc, inline.clj, db.cljc, impl/entity.cljc, built_ins.cljc, parser.cljc,
  pull_parser.cljc, pull_api.cljc, query.cljc                  -> src/datascript/
  me/tonsky/persistent_sorted_set/arrays.cljc                  -> src/me/tonsky/persistent_sorted_set/arrays.cljc
  me/tonsky/persistent_sorted_set.cljs                         -> src/me/tonsky/persistent_sorted_set.clj

Not taken: datascript.core and what only it loads — conn (its Conn is extend-clj's deftype-atom, a JVM library),
storage (java.io, java.lang.ref), serialize, pprint (clojure.pprint), datafy, js, query_v3. The workload calls the
namespaces core delegates to (bench/workloads/src/workloads/datascript.clj).

What is ported, and why. This runtime reads the :clj branches (corpus-bench's features are #{:clj}); there the
index is persistent-sorted-set's Java classes, and datascript's types implement JVM interfaces and Object. Every
change is a `pippin:` comment at its place, and pippin.diff is the whole diff against the jars' files. What the
workload reaches behaves as upstream (its result is the JVM's and ClojureScript's, checked with = on every run);
what behaves otherwise, or not at all, is named below.

- persistent_sorted_set.clj is the ClojureScript implementation (B+ tree of arrays, branching 32 where the Java one
  takes 512) with its cljs protocols spelled as the JVM interfaces this runtime's deftype implements (ISeqable ->
  Seqable seq, IReduce -> IReduceInit reduce, ILookup -> valAt ...); js/Math constants as longs, Math.floor of a
  division as a floor quot, .slice as aslice, cljs's ^:mutable _hash as ^:unsynchronized-mutable, its caching-hash
  macro spelled out. Not carried: the chunked seq (Chunk: no chunked seqs here), toString and the printer, -clone,
  -empty, -disjoin and the transient protocols: a deftype has no slot behind IEditableCollection or
  ITransientCollection, and transient, conj! and persistent! are the persistent operations here, so a transient of a
  BTSet is the set and conj! reaches its conj, which is all the cljs methods do. rseq of a slice goes through a
  protocol of the file's own: a deftype has no Reversible slot.
- arrays.cljc: object-array, aget/aset/alength, loops for System/arraycopy and Arrays/copyOf, sort for
  Arrays/parallelSort, the array type for .getClass/.isArray.
- db.cljc: no clojure.data (DB's Diff and EqualityPartition go); defrecord-updatable keeps the protocols only, since
  a record here takes protocols only: DB and FilteredDB hash, compare, count and empty as records do, not as
  datascript overrides (the datom set's hash, its count); Datom keeps IHashEq, Seqable, IPersistentCollection
  (equiv, count, cons) and ILookup, and loses Object (toString, hashCode: hasheq is hashCode's hash-datom cached in
  _hash), empty, Indexed and Associative (nth, find, contains? and assoc of a datom do not work here); AutoTempid
  loses Object toString; defcomp makes a fn, as for cljs,
  where the JVM reifies java.util.Comparator; .compareTo and .equals are compare and =, class is type,
  Util/hashCombine and Util/hasheq are hash-combine and hash; patch-tag drops cljs's boolean and number tags.
- impl/entity.cljc: Entity keeps IHashEq, Seqable, IPersistentCollection (equiv, count, cons), ILookup and IFn,
  and loses Object and Associative (contains?, find and assoc of an entity do not work here); its hash has no
  System/identityHashCode of the db, which = does not need.
- lru.cljc: LRU keeps ILookup; cache calls assoc-lru, which LRU's Associative assoc is.
- query.cljc, pull_api.cljc: da/array? for .getClass .isArray, get for .valAt, vec for LazilyPersistentVector,
  first, next and cons for ISeq's methods, read-string for clojure.edn's (no clojure.edn here).
- util.cljc: log expands as on a JVM without -Ddatascript.debug.

Load failures left (the harness loads leniently; the workload reaches none of them): squuid (UUID/randomUUID),
dedupe-interfaces (IllegalArgumentException., unused by the ported defrecord-updatable), and the four top-level
(set! *warn-on-reflection* ...) and (set! *unchecked-math* ...) forms.

The language gaps behind the port are NOTES entries: "Type descriptor" (Indexed and Associative on a deftype, the
transient interfaces, a Reversible slot, Object methods), "Records" (a record's own hash, = and count), "Corpus" (clojure.data,
clojure.edn). There is no manifest.edn: this directory is not a corpus library with a suite of its own, and
bench/workloads/datascript/manifest.edn is its root for corpus-bench's clj-facts.
